## Scope and result

Read-only public-primary-source refresh for samcday/pocketfed#58 and the September 14 research, performed on September 28, 2026. No hardware access, builds, upstream messages, or repository mutations. The researched software is upstream ModemManager/libqmi; branch heads below identify the inspected revisions. Hardware results quoted below are the authors' reports, not independent PocketFed validation.

**The backend landscape changed.** Three public, unmerged EpicLPer patches appeared September 24–26: libqmi !476 (NAS dual-standby control), libqmi !478 (UIM Subscription OK), and ModemManager !1504 (initial primary subscription bootstrap). They are concrete reusable experiments to track. None establishes working Sargo DSDS, a shared desktop subscription API, or per-call/per-message routing. No inspected source identifies them as Guido's NLnet work.

## New reusable work

- [libqmi !476](https://gitlab.freedesktop.org/mobile-broadband/libqmi/-/merge_requests/476), opened 2026-09-24T15:20:53.014Z, last updated 2026-09-24T15:26:35.926Z, open. Source [EpicLPer/libqmi, nas-dual-standby-preference](https://gitlab.freedesktop.org/EpicLPer/libqmi/-/tree/nas-dual-standby-preference), head `b34da8c6d7e0a4541da7935c8998a422ee44277f`; API/message commit `6c03630060590114a8739e1d7bb0d31f89d63904`. Two commits based on upstream `b7913df8b49330956f0337dcc6255f63751fdda1`. Inspected diff adds NAS Set Dual Standby Preference (0x004B), Get (0x005C), indication (0x0047), enums, and qmicli get/set commands. Fields include standby/priority, default data/voice subscriptions, and active-subscriptions mask. This is lower-level modem control, not GNOME preference policy. Author reports Lumia 950 XL/MSM8994 kernel 7.2 bring-up: setting a single primary active bit restored cell camping; generated request encoding checked. That is not a demonstrated two-line standby/calling result. CI pipeline [1753251](https://gitlab.freedesktop.org/EpicLPer/libqmi/-/pipelines/1753251) succeeds. MR has zero user notes.
- [libqmi !478](https://gitlab.freedesktop.org/mobile-broadband/libqmi/-/merge_requests/478), opened 2026-09-26T07:54:36.059Z, updated 2026-09-26T07:54:51.106Z, open. Source [EpicLPer/libqmi, uim-subscription-ok](https://gitlab.freedesktop.org/EpicLPer/libqmi/-/tree/uim-subscription-ok), head `97ff0b1738ce594595cb4503375b290958af9f2b`. Adds UIM Subscription OK (0x0040), allowing the host to release a subscription halted by modem configuration. Author reports card application reaching ready on Lumia 950 XL. CI [1754570](https://gitlab.freedesktop.org/EpicLPer/libqmi/-/pipelines/1754570) succeeds; zero user notes.
- [ModemManager !1504](https://gitlab.freedesktop.org/mobile-broadband/ModemManager/-/merge_requests/1504), opened 2026-09-26T07:56:45.683Z, updated 2026-09-26T08:09:03.836Z, open. Source [EpicLPer/ModemManager, select-sim-application](https://gitlab.freedesktop.org/EpicLPer/ModemManager/-/tree/select-sim-application), head `5860ed80d98f64a560e7670c9011b6240483dce5`; first commit `cbbfad49bf8224d8dc71f2124da14fc22a236c77`. Based on upstream `338ecc06f294d57edea003b866080aacb4055917`. Inspected diff chooses the first present USIM for primary-GW provisioning when none is bound, then handles halted subscription publishing. It leaves an existing primary-GW binding alone and does not implement secondary provisioning or a persisted user preference. Author reports MM loading the SIM on Lumia 950 XL with its separate vendor helper disabled. It explicitly addresses MM #649 and depends on **libqmi !478**, not !476; !476 and !478 are separate sibling branches from the same upstream base. The MR notes its libqmi version requirement still needs updating once the API is released. CI [1754572](https://gitlab.freedesktop.org/EpicLPer/ModemManager/-/pipelines/1754572) fails. Public job metadata shows failures including build-debug, build-release, and build-qmi-qrtr-no-mbim; build-asan and several no-QMI variants pass. The build-debug trace endpoint returned HTTP 401, so the exact failure cause was not established. One user note exists, but notes are inaccessible anonymously.

All three source branch names and exact head SHAs were separately verified through the GitLab repository-branches API; they are obtainable public branches, not just issue ideas. The new APIs use 1.40 annotations; that is not evidence libqmi 1.40 has been released.

