## Practical conclusion for PocketFed #58

Track !476 for future read-only NAS state inspection and controlled Qualcomm experiments. Track !1504 + !478 as potential upstream replacement for some initial provisioning script duties, while retaining the distinction between first-card fallback and PocketFed's selected-card policy. Review/port only when resuming the hardware work; no reason to ship these automatically during session closeout. None changes the prior recommendation to align the full subscription architecture with Guido instead of building a competing desktop model.

